Introduction

1.1 Purpose

This document specifies the Software Requirements Specification (SRS) for MiniOS Ver-
sion 4.0.

MiniOS is a pedagogical operating system built by extending the xv6 UNIX-like teach-
ing OS. The system demonstrates scheduling, memory management, file management,
garbage collection, and dynamic memory compaction mechanisms.

1.2 Document Conventions

Requirements are labeled:

REQ-SCH-* (Scheduling)
REQ-MEM-* (Memory)
REQ-FILE-* (File Manager)
REQ-GC-* (Garbage Collector)
REQ-DMEM-* (Dynamic Memory Compaction)

1.3 Intended Audience and Reading Suggestions

This document is intended for:

• OS Developers

• Academic Evaluators

• System Testers

• Project Supervisors

Readers should begin with Section 2 (Overall Description) before proceeding to System
Features.

1.4 Product Scope

MiniOS extends xv6 to demonstrate:

• Priority-based scheduling with aging

• Paging with Copy-On-Write

• File management subsystem

• Garbage collection

• Dynamic memory compaction

